#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wake each agent whose turn an open issue or pull request is.

Nothing else tells an agent that it is its turn. This reads every open
issue and pull request with one GraphQL query, asks the project's rules
whose turn each is, and sends each agent one XMPP message, through the
host's webhook relay (xmpp-mcp's `xmpp-webhook-relay`), listing the
items that became its turn.

**The rules** are a module the configuration names in `router.rules`:
`"default"`, the rules shipped here and the default, or a file in the
project's own checkout, relative to its root. This is the engine every
project shares: fetching, locking, state, the once-per-turn key,
reminders, delivery and the journal. The rules say what a turn is and
whom it falls to; agent_forge/rules_default.py lists the default ones,
and agent_forge/router.py and docs/router.md the interface. The query
asks for each item's number and what the rules declare, and each lookup
the rules declare runs after it (the default rules' finds what each
`Blocked-by:` line names).

**What the rules decide.** For each open item, `decide` gives any
number of decisions, and `sweep`, once a run, more: about items or
about none (a red default branch, say). Each has a kind. A **turn** is
the agent's to act on. A **notice** (for its information) and a
**relook** (worth looking at again) are sent too, each in its own
section marked not the agent's turn. A **surface** wakes nobody: it is
printed on every run, sending or not, and journalled once (the default
rules' rule 7, a pull request nobody can review). A decision may carry
**actions**, such as adding a label (`router.AddLabel`): a sending run
does them as the Merger's App before delivery, when the decision is
due, and a dry run prints them. A failed action is printed and
journalled, and the wake still goes out.

**Who is woken.** A turn that falls to someone not in the
configuration's `agents`, such as the owner's own pull request, is
printed and logged once, and not sent. Nobody's turn is forgotten, and
printed in a dry run. A wake is addressed to the agent's session name:
the entry's `session_name`, else `naming.session_prefix` and its name.

**Once per turn.** A turn's key is (agent, item, the event that started
it, as the rules say); a decision about no item has "-" and its rule in
the item's place. The rule is otherwise recorded but is not part of the
key: rules that mean the same thing can hand one turn between them, and
a label coming off is enough to do it. `state.json` in the state
directory records, per item, each turn last woken, when, and how many
reminders it has had (one turn as an object, several as a list of
them). A turn is woken when its key is new, and again only as a
reminder: by the decision's `router.Reminder` (a first interval,
doubling to a ceiling, delayed by a jitter fixed by the key), or, with
none, once `relay.remind_seconds` (default 7200;
`$FORGE_ROUTER_REMIND` overrides it) have passed. `wakes.jsonl`
appends every wake sent, failed, withheld or withdrawn, with the
reason.

**Check before send.** When the rules have a `recheck` of their own
(not `decide` itself, as the default rules'), a sending run fetches
each item it is about to wake for again, in one query, and re-decides
it just before delivery. A wake whose item no longer has a decision for
its agent and event is not sent, is journalled as withdrawn on
recheck, and isn't recorded; a recheck that can't be fetched leaves its
wakes unsent and due.

**One message per agent per run**, posted verbatim (`X-XMPP-Verbatim:
1`, `text/plain`, `X-Webhook-Token` from `relay.token_file`, default
`~/.config/xmpp-webhook-relay/token`) to `/agent/<session name>` on the
relay at `relay.url` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8788`;
`$FORGE_ROUTER_RELAY` overrides it). The relay resolves the name
against the room its agents share. A wake counts as delivered only
when the relay says it took exactly that message: a `200` whose answer
is `"status": "queued"` with one target, or `"duplicate"` (it already
took this delivery). Anything else leaves every item in the message
due, and the next run tries again; state is written only for what was
delivered. The run says which fault it was:

* a `404` saying `unknown-name` is the relay's: no session of that name
  is in the room now. Any other `404` isn't the relay speaking, so
  `relay.url` is wrong, a different fault from an absent agent;
* a `503` asking to retry within RELAY_RETRY_MAX_S seconds
  (`Retry-After`; its queue is full, or it hasn't loaded the room yet)
  is tried once more, under the same `X-Webhook-Delivery` ID, so the
  relay can't deliver it twice. Each message's ID is fixed for the run
  and new the next run, so a later wake of the same text isn't taken
  for a duplicate;
* no answer at all means the relay is down: nothing more is posted to
  it this run, and every remaining wake stays due.

**The directory.** Rules whose `wants_directory` is true (the default
rules' idle offer, `router.idle_offer`) are handed the relay's `GET
/directory` answer as `ctx.directory`: who is in the agents' room,
and busy or idle since when. It is read once a run, with the same
token as a post, sending or not. An answer that isn't a complete
directory is printed (`NO-DIRECTORY: …`) and handed over as None,
which the rules read as unknown, never as idle.

**Without `--send` it is a dry run**: it prints each decision and the
messages it would send, sends nothing, takes no lock and leaves
`state.json` alone. It appends each turn it would send or withhold to
`dry-run.jsonl`, once per turn key (`dry-state.json` remembers which),
so its decisions can be compared with what happened. `--only N[,N]`
routes those items alone, for a run started by one event: the sweep
is told them (`ctx.only`), and any decision about another item, or
about none, is dropped. A sending
run holds an exclusive `flock` on `lock` in the state directory across
read, decide, send and write, so cron's runs and an event's runs never
wake the same turn twice; one that can't have it
within LOCK_WAIT_S says BUSY and exits 0.

GitHub is read as the Merger's App. The state directory is
~/.local/state/agent-forge/<project>/router; the configuration is the
cron checkout's (`$FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT`).

Exit 0 when nothing was due or all of it was delivered (and for a dry
run, and BUSY); 1 when some was delivered and the rest stays due; 2
when something was due and none of it was delivered, or the question
could not be asked (no token, GitHub failed, the rules couldn't be
loaded or decided something this can't carry out).
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import fcntl
import hashlib
import http.client
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(BIN))
from agent_forge import config, locks, router  # noqa: E402


def _load(name, path):
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(name, path)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


# The Merger's `gh api` wrapper, its token minting and its state files,
# and, through `configure`, the rules' use of its tests, so the two
# never disagree.
merger = _load("forge_merger", os.path.join(BIN, "forge-merger"))

# Set from the project's configuration by `configure`.
REPO_SLUG = ""
ACT_AS = "Merger"
# The rules module `router.rules` names.
RULES = None
DEFAULT_RELAY = "http://127.0.0.1:8788"
RELAY = DEFAULT_RELAY
DEFAULT_TOKEN_FILE = "~/.config/xmpp-webhook-relay/token"
TOKEN_FILE = os.path.expanduser(DEFAULT_TOKEN_FILE)
DEFAULT_REMIND_S = 7200
REMIND_S = DEFAULT_REMIND_S
POST_TIMEOUT_S = 15
# The longest Retry-After a 503 may ask for and still be tried again in
# the same run; a longer one waits for the next run.
RELAY_RETRY_MAX_S = 10
# How a poster's reason starts when the relay gave no answer at all.
UNREACHABLE = "relay unreachable"
# Seconds a sending run waits for another's lock before saying BUSY.
LOCK_WAIT_S = 60

# The engine's query: each open item's number, and what the rules ask
# for (`graphql`, by type).
QUERY = """
query($owner:String!, $name:String!, $prCursor:String, $issueCursor:String,
      $prs:Boolean!, $issues:Boolean!) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
    pullRequests(states:OPEN, first:30, after:$prCursor) @include(if:$prs) {
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
      nodes {
        number %(PullRequest)s
      }
    }
    issues(states:OPEN, first:50, after:$issueCursor) @include(if:$issues) {
      pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
      nodes {
        number %(Issue)s
      }
    }
  }
}"""


def configure(project, rules=True):
    """Set the module's settings, the Merger's and, with `rules`, the
    rules' from `project`. Raises router.RulesError when `router.rules`
    names no rules module. The Merger borrows only the poster, so it
    loads no rules: a project's rules file is no business of its."""
    global REPO_SLUG, ACT_AS, RULES, RELAY, TOKEN_FILE, REMIND_S
    merger.configure(project)
    relay = project.section("relay")
    REPO_SLUG = project.repo
    ACT_AS = merger.ACT_AS
    RELAY = relay.get("url", DEFAULT_RELAY)
    TOKEN_FILE = os.path.expanduser(relay.get("token_file",
                                              DEFAULT_TOKEN_FILE))
    REMIND_S = relay.get("remind_seconds", DEFAULT_REMIND_S)
    if not rules:
        return
    module = router.load_rules(project.section("router").get(
        "rules", router.DEFAULT_RULES), project.root)
    module.configure(project, merger)
    RULES = module


def parse_time(stamp):
    return datetime.datetime.strptime(stamp, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(
        tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)


# --- GitHub -----------------------------------------------------------------


def prepare(node, typename):
    """`node` as the rules see it: the `flatten` connections as lists and
    `__typename` set."""
    for field in RULES.flatten:
        if isinstance(node.get(field), dict):
            node[field] = node[field].get("nodes") or []
    node["__typename"] = typename
    return node


def fetch(github):
    """(pull requests, issues): every open one, as GraphQL's nodes with
    the rules' `flatten` connections as lists and `__typename` set, then
    what the rules' lookups attach."""
    owner, name = REPO_SLUG.split("/")
    query = QUERY % {"PullRequest": RULES.graphql.get("PullRequest", ""),
                     "Issue": RULES.graphql.get("Issue", "")}
    prs, issues = [], []
    cursors = {"prCursor": None, "issueCursor": None}
    more = {"prs": True, "issues": True}
    while more["prs"] or more["issues"]:
        args = ["graphql", "-f", "query=" + query, "-F", "owner=" + owner,
                "-F", "name=" + name,
                "-F", "prs=%s" % str(more["prs"]).lower(),
                "-F", "issues=%s" % str(more["issues"]).lower()]
        for key, cursor in cursors.items():
            if cursor:
                args += ["-f", "%s=%s" % (key, cursor)]
        repo = github.api(*args)["data"]["repository"]
        for kind, conn, out, cursor, typename in (
                ("prs", "pullRequests", prs, "prCursor", "PullRequest"),
                ("issues", "issues", issues, "issueCursor", "Issue")):
            if not more[kind]:
                continue
            page = repo[conn]
            for node in page["nodes"]:
                out.append(prepare(node, typename))
            more[kind] = page["pageInfo"]["hasNextPage"]
            cursors[cursor] = page["pageInfo"]["endCursor"]
    for lookup in RULES.lookups:
        lookup.run(github, REPO_SLUG, prs, issues)
    return prs, issues


# The recheck's query: the numbered items alone, as they are now.
RECHECK_QUERY = """
query($owner:String!, $name:String!) {
  repository(owner:$owner, name:$name) {
%s
  }
}"""
RECHECK_FIELD = """    n%(n)d: issueOrPullRequest(number:%(n)d) {
      __typename
      ... on PullRequest { number state %(PullRequest)s }
      ... on Issue { number state %(Issue)s }
    }"""


def refetch(github, numbers):
    """{number: node} for those of `numbers` still open, fetched afresh
    in one query, prepared as `fetch` prepares them and with the rules'
    lookups run over them. One closed, merged or gone is left out.
    Raises whatever the query or a lookup raises."""
    owner, name = REPO_SLUG.split("/")
    fields = {"PullRequest": RULES.graphql.get("PullRequest", ""),
              "Issue": RULES.graphql.get("Issue", "")}
    query = RECHECK_QUERY % "\n".join(
        RECHECK_FIELD % dict(fields, n=n) for n in numbers)
    repo = github.api("graphql", "-f", "query=" + query, "-F",
                      "owner=" + owner, "-F", "name=" + name
                      )["data"]["repository"]
    prs, issues = [], []
    for n in numbers:
        node = repo.get("n%d" % n)
        if not node or node.get("state") != "OPEN":
            continue
        typename = node.get("__typename")
        if typename not in ("PullRequest", "Issue"):
            continue
        (prs if typename == "PullRequest" else issues).append(
            prepare(node, typename))
    for lookup in RULES.lookups:
        lookup.run(github, REPO_SLUG, prs, issues)
    return {node["number"]: node for node in prs + issues}


# --- state and wakes --------------------------------------------------------


# What makes a turn new, with the item: the rule is recorded beside
# them, not compared.
TURN_FIELDS = ("agent", "event")


def key_of(decision):
    return {"agent": decision.agent, "rule": decision.rule,
            "event": decision.event}


def item_key(decision):
    """Where `state.json` keeps a decision's turns: its item's number,
    or, for one about no item, "-" and its rule, which a module keeps
    stable from run to run."""
    if decision.item is None:
        return "-%s" % (decision.rule,)
    return str(decision.item)


def label(decision):
    """How the output names what a decision is about."""
    if decision.item is None:
        return item_key(decision)
    return "#%d" % decision.item


def turn_id(decision):
    """The turn's whole key, (agent, item, event), as one string: what a
    `Reminder`'s jitter hashes."""
    return json.dumps([decision.agent, item_key(decision), decision.event])


def same_turn(entry, decision):
    """Whether `entry`, as recorded for `decision`'s item, is
    `decision`'s turn."""
    key = key_of(decision)
    return isinstance(entry, dict) and bool(entry) and all(
        entry.get(k) == key[k] for k in TURN_FIELDS)


def entries(items, key):
    """The turns recorded under an item key. One turn is recorded as a
    dict, the only form before several per item, and several as a list
    of them, so a state file from before still reads as it did."""
    value = items.get(key)
    if isinstance(value, dict):
        return [value] if value else []
    if isinstance(value, list):
        return [e for e in value if isinstance(e, dict) and e]
    return []


def put_entries(items, key, turns):
    """Record `turns` under an item key, in the form `entries` reads."""
    if not turns:
        items.pop(key, None)
    elif len(turns) == 1:
        items[key] = turns[0]
    else:
        items[key] = list(turns)


def find(items, decision):
    """The recorded entry of `decision`'s turn, or None."""
    return next((e for e in entries(items, item_key(decision))
                 if same_turn(e, decision)), None)


def record(items, decision, entry):
    """Record `entry` as `decision`'s turn, in place of what was."""
    key = item_key(decision)
    put_entries(items, key, [e for e in entries(items, key)
                             if not same_turn(e, decision)] + [entry])


def prune(items, live, only, held=()):
    """Keep only the turns this run still decided: an item key's
    entries not matching one of `live[key]` are forgotten, and so is an
    item key not decided at all, unless the run was `only` some items.
    A key in `held` had a wake that stays due, and is left as it was, as
    a failed wake always has been."""
    for key in list(items):
        if key in held:
            continue
        if key in live:
            put_entries(items, key, [e for e in entries(items, key)
                                     if any(same_turn(e, d)
                                            for d in live[key])])
        elif not only:
            del items[key]


def reminders_sent(entry):
    try:
        return max(int((entry or {}).get("reminders") or 0), 0)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return 0


def due(decision, entry, when, remind_s):
    """None when `decision`'s turn needs no wake now; "new" for a key
    not woken before; "reminder" for one woken long enough ago: by the
    decision's `Reminder`, or `remind_s` when it has none."""
    if not same_turn(entry, decision):
        return "new"
    if entry.get("withheld") or entry.get("surfaced"):
        return None
    try:
        woken = parse_time(entry["woken_at"])
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return "new"
    wait = remind_s if decision.reminder is None else decision.reminder.wait(
        turn_id(decision), reminders_sent(entry))
    return "reminder" if (when - woken).total_seconds() >= wait else None


# The message's sections after its turns, by kind: what the agent is told
# about without its being the agent's turn.
SECTIONS = (("notice", "For your information (not your turn):"),
            ("relook", "Worth another look (not your turn):"))


def message(lines, notices=(), relooks=()):
    """The text of one agent's wake: its turns, under the heading a
    wake has always had, then each other section that has lines."""
    parts = [(heading, body) for heading, body in (
        ("Your turn:", lines), (SECTIONS[0][1], notices),
        (SECTIONS[1][1], relooks)) if body]
    return "From: Router\n" + "\n".join(
        heading + "\n" + "\n".join(body) + "\n" for heading, body in parts)


def relay_token(path=None):
    """The relay's shared token from its environment file, or None."""
    path = path or TOKEN_FILE
    try:
        with open(path) as handle:
            for line in handle:
                key, _, value = line.strip().partition("=")
                if key.strip() == "WEBHOOK_TOKEN" and value.strip():
                    return value.strip().strip("'\"")
    except OSError:
        pass
    return None


def delivery_id(session, text, stamp):
    """X-Webhook-Delivery: the same for a retry within one run, different
    for the next run's wake of the same text."""
    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps([session, text, stamp]).encode()
                          ).hexdigest()[:32]


def relay_answer(raw):
    """The relay's JSON answer as a dict, or {} for anything else."""
    try:
        answer = json.loads(raw or b"{}")
    except (ValueError, UnicodeDecodeError):
        return {}
    return answer if isinstance(answer, dict) else {}


def accepted(answer):
    """Whether a 200's answer says the relay took exactly this message."""
    return (answer.get("status") == "duplicate"
            or (answer.get("status") == "queued"
                and len(answer.get("targets") or []) == 1))


def make_poster(relay, token, opener=urllib.request.urlopen, sleep=time.sleep,
                stamp=None):
    """A function (session name, text) -> None when the relay took the
    message, else why not (see the module docstring). A reason starting
    UNREACHABLE means the relay gave no answer. No reason ever contains
    the token."""
    stamp = repr(time.time()) if stamp is None else stamp
    base = relay.rstrip("/")

    def attempt(req):
        """(status, answer dict, retry-after header or None)."""
        try:
            with opener(req, timeout=POST_TIMEOUT_S) as resp:
                read = getattr(resp, "read", None)
                return resp.status, relay_answer(read(2000) if read else b""), None
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as err:
            try:
                raw = err.read(2000)
            except (AttributeError, OSError):
                raw = b""
            headers = err.headers or {}
            return err.code, relay_answer(raw), headers.get("Retry-After")

    def post(session, text):
        if not token:
            return "no relay token in %s" % TOKEN_FILE
        url = "%s/agent/%s" % (base, urllib.parse.quote(session, safe=""))
        req = urllib.request.Request(
            url, data=text.encode("utf-8"), method="POST",
            headers={"X-Webhook-Token": token, "X-XMPP-Verbatim": "1",
                     "X-Webhook-Delivery": delivery_id(session, text, stamp),
                     "Content-Type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8"})
        try:
            code, answer, retry = attempt(req)
            if code == 503:
                try:
                    wait = float(retry) if retry is not None else None
                except ValueError:
                    wait = None
                if wait is not None and 0 <= wait <= RELAY_RETRY_MAX_S:
                    sleep(wait)
                    code, answer, retry = attempt(req)
        except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as err:
            # HTTPException too: a relay killed mid-answer raises
            # IncompleteRead or BadStatusLine, which aren't OSErrors.
            return "%s: %s" % (UNREACHABLE, getattr(err, "reason", err))
        reason = answer.get("reason")
        if code == 200:
            return None if accepted(answer) else (
                "HTTP 200, but not the relay's answer for one message")
        if code == 404 and reason == "unknown-name":
            return "HTTP 404 unknown-name: no session %s in the room" % session
        if code == 404:
            return ("HTTP 404, not the relay's: is relay.url (%s) the relay?"
                    % base)
        return "HTTP %d%s" % (code, " " + reason if reason else "")

    return post


def make_directory_reader(relay, token, opener=urllib.request.urlopen):
    """A function () -> (the relay's `GET /directory` answer, None), or
    (None, why not). Only a complete answer counts: a `200` whose JSON
    has `"complete": true` and a list of `agents`. Anything else (no
    token, a 503 while the relay loads its room, no answer) is "unknown",
    which the rules must never read as "nobody is there". No reason ever
    contains the token."""
    url = relay.rstrip("/") + "/directory"

    def read():
        if not token:
            return None, "no relay token in %s" % TOKEN_FILE
        req = urllib.request.Request(url, method="GET",
                                     headers={"X-Webhook-Token": token})
        try:
            with opener(req, timeout=POST_TIMEOUT_S) as resp:
                code, raw = resp.status, resp.read(1000000)
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as err:
            return None, "HTTP %d" % err.code
        except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError,
                http.client.HTTPException) as err:
            return None, "%s: %s" % (UNREACHABLE, getattr(err, "reason", err))
        answer = relay_answer(raw)
        if code != 200 or answer.get("complete") is not True \
                or not isinstance(answer.get("agents"), list):
            return None, "HTTP %d, not a complete directory" % code
        return answer, None

    return read


def check(decision):
    """Raise ValueError for a decision this engine can't carry out: the
    rules are wrong, and half-doing it would be worse."""
    d = decision
    problem = None
    if not isinstance(d, router.Decision):
        problem = "not a Decision"
    elif d.item is not None and (not isinstance(d.item, int)
                                 or isinstance(d.item, bool)):
        problem = "its item is not a number or None"
    elif d.kind not in router.KINDS:
        problem = "its kind is not one of %s" % ", ".join(router.KINDS)
    elif not isinstance(d.actions, tuple) or not all(
            isinstance(a, router.Action) for a in d.actions):
        problem = "its actions are not a tuple of Actions"
    elif d.reminder is not None and not isinstance(d.reminder,
                                                   router.Reminder):
        problem = "its reminder is not a Reminder"
    elif d.actions and d.agent is None and d.kind != "surface":
        problem = "nobody's turn has no key to do its actions once for"
    elif (d.agent is not None and d.suppressed is None
          and d.kind != "surface" and not isinstance(d.line, str)):
        problem = "a wake needs a line"
    if problem:
        raise ValueError("the rules decided %r, which this router can't "
                         "carry out: %s" % (d, problem))


def decide(ctx):
    """Every decision the rules make: `decide` for each open item, pull
    requests first, then `sweep` once, each checked. A second decision
    with the key of one before it (agent, item, event) is the same turn,
    and is dropped."""
    decisions = []
    for item in ctx.prs + ctx.issues:
        decisions += RULES.decide(item, ctx)
    decisions += RULES.sweep(ctx)
    kept, seen = [], set()
    for d in decisions:
        check(d)
        if d.agent is not None or d.kind == "surface":
            key = turn_id(d)
            if key in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(key)
        kept.append(d)
    return kept


def order(decision):
    """Items by number, then those about no item, each in decided order."""
    return (decision.item is None, decision.item or 0)


def nobody_line(d):
    """How a decision that wakes nobody is printed."""
    why = d.suppressed if d.suppressed is not None else d.line
    return "%s %s (%s)" % (label(d), "nobody's" if d.agent is None
                           else "%s's" % d.agent,
                           why if d.rule is None
                           else "rule %s: %s" % (d.rule, why))


def journal(d, line, outcome, **extra):
    """One record for `wakes.jsonl` or `dry-run.jsonl`."""
    entry = dict(key_of(d), item=d.item, line=line, outcome=outcome)
    if d.kind != "turn":
        entry["kind"] = d.kind
    entry.update(extra)
    return entry


def act(github, d, send, out):
    """Do `d`'s actions, in order, as the Merger's App, or, in a dry run,
    print them. Returns what happened to each, for the journal. A failed
    action is reported and the rest go on: the wake still goes out."""
    done = []
    for action in d.actions:
        what = action.describe()
        if not send:
            out("WOULD %s" % what)
            done.append("would " + what)
            continue
        try:
            ok, why = action.run(github, REPO_SLUG)
        except Exception as err:  # noqa: BLE001 - an action never stops a run
            ok, why = False, str(err)
        if ok:
            out("DONE %s" % what)
            done.append(what)
        else:
            out("ACTION FAILED: %s: %s" % (what, why))
            done.append("failed: %s: %s" % (what, why))
    return done


def rechecks():
    """Whether the rules re-decide before delivery: a `recheck` of their
    own, not the default that is `decide` itself."""
    return RULES.recheck is not RULES.decide


def recheck(github, ctx, wakes):
    """Re-decide, on a fresh fetch, each item `wakes` would wake for.
    Returns (wakes that still hold, [(wake, why)] withdrawn, [(wake,
    why)] that couldn't be rechecked and stay due). A wake holds when
    the fresh decisions give its item a decision with its agent and
    event. A wake about no item is sent as decided."""
    numbers = sorted({w["d"].item for w in wakes if w["d"].item is not None})
    if not numbers:
        return wakes, [], []
    try:
        fresh = refetch(github, numbers)
    except Exception as err:  # noqa: BLE001 - gh's and lookups' failures vary
        return ([w for w in wakes if w["d"].item is None], [],
                [(w, "recheck failed: %s" % err) for w in wakes
                 if w["d"].item is not None])

    def renewed(nodes):
        return [fresh.get(n["number"]) if n["number"] in numbers else n
                for n in nodes
                if n["number"] not in numbers or n["number"] in fresh]
    now = router.Context(ctx.roster, ctx.when, renewed(ctx.prs),
                         renewed(ctx.issues), only=ctx.only,
                         directory=ctx.directory)
    again = {n: list(RULES.recheck(fresh[n], now)) if n in fresh else []
             for n in numbers}
    holding, withdrawn = [], []
    for w in wakes:
        d = w["d"]
        if d.item is None or any(
                r.agent == d.agent and r.event == d.event
                and item_key(r) == item_key(d) for r in again[d.item]):
            holding.append(w)
        else:
            withdrawn.append((w, "closed" if d.item not in fresh
                              else "no longer decided"))
    return holding, withdrawn, []


def run(github, roster, state_dir, send, post=None, only=None, out=print,
        when=None, remind_s=None, directory=None):
    """One run: decide every open item, or `only` those numbers, and
    when `send`, do the due decisions' actions, wake each agent with
    its due items and record it. `directory`, for rules that want it,
    reads the relay's directory (`make_directory_reader`). Returns the
    exit status: 0 when nothing was due or all of it was delivered, 1
    when some was and the rest stays due, 2 when something was due and
    none of it was delivered."""
    when = when or merger.now_utc()
    remind_s = REMIND_S if remind_s is None else remind_s
    prs, issues = fetch(github)
    listing = None
    if RULES.wants_directory and directory is not None:
        listing, why = directory()
        if listing is None:
            out("NO-DIRECTORY: %s; nobody is taken to be idle" % why)
    ctx = router.Context(roster, when, prs, issues,
                         only=frozenset(only) if only else None,
                         directory=listing)
    decisions = decide(ctx)
    tally = RULES.summary(ctx)
    if only:
        decisions = [d for d in decisions if d.item in only]
    decisions.sort(key=order)
    state_path = os.path.join(state_dir, "state.json")
    state = merger.load_json(state_path, {})
    items = state.get("items")
    if not isinstance(items, dict):
        items = state["items"] = {}
    # `live`: the decisions, by item key, whose recorded turns are kept.
    # `acting`: decisions recorded once (withheld, surfaced) whose
    # actions are done now, with their journal record.
    log, would, wakes, acting, live = [], [], [], [], {}
    for d in decisions:
        keep = live.setdefault(item_key(d), [])
        if d.kind == "surface":
            out(nobody_line(d))
            keep.append(d)
            outcome = "surfaced: %s" % (
                d.suppressed if d.suppressed is not None else d.line)
            # The dry run's journal keeps its own once-per-key.
            would.append((d, d.line, outcome))
            if find(items, d) is None:
                record(items, d, dict(key_of(d), surfaced=True,
                                      at=merger.iso(when)))
                rec = journal(d, d.line, outcome)
                log.append(rec)
                acting.append((d, rec))
            continue
        if d.agent is None or d.suppressed is not None:
            if not send:
                out(nobody_line(d))
            continue
        keep.append(d)
        entry = find(items, d)
        why = due(d, entry, when, remind_s)
        if why is None:
            if not send:
                out("%s %s's, rule %s: already woken" % (
                    label(d), d.agent, d.rule))
                would.append((d, d.line, "withheld: already woken"))
            continue
        if not roster.is_agent(d.agent):
            out("%s %s's, rule %s: withheld, %s is not an agent" % (
                label(d), d.agent, d.rule, d.agent))
            record(items, d, dict(key_of(d), withheld=True,
                                  at=merger.iso(when)))
            rec = journal(d, d.line, "withheld: not an agent")
            log.append(rec)
            acting.append((d, rec))
            would.append((d, d.line, "withheld: not an agent"))
            continue
        line = d.line + (" (reminder)" if why == "reminder" else "")
        would.append((d, line, "would send to %s" % roster.session_name(
            d.agent)))
        wakes.append({"d": d, "line": line, "why": why, "entry": entry})
    # Item keys with a wake that stays due, and how much was delivered.
    held, delivered, stayed, withdrawn_n, unchecked_n = set(), 0, 0, 0, 0
    if send and wakes and rechecks():
        wakes, withdrawn, unchecked = recheck(github, ctx, wakes)
        for w, why in withdrawn:
            d = w["d"]
            withdrawn_n += 1
            out("%s %s's, rule %s: withdrawn on recheck (%s)" % (
                label(d), d.agent, d.rule, why))
            live[item_key(d)].remove(d)
            log.append(journal(d, w["line"], "withdrawn on recheck: " + why))
        for w, why in unchecked:
            d = w["d"]
            stayed += 1
            unchecked_n += 1
            held.add(item_key(d))
            out("NOT SENT %s to %s: %s; it stays due" % (
                label(d), roster.session_name(d.agent), why))
            log.append(journal(d, w["line"], "not sent: " + why,
                               session=roster.session_name(d.agent)))
    for d, rec in acting:
        if d.actions:
            rec["actions"] = act(github, d, send, out)
    for w in wakes:
        w["actions"] = act(github, w["d"], send, out) if w["d"].actions \
            else None
    batches = {}
    for w in wakes:
        batches.setdefault(w["d"].agent, []).append(w)
    failed, down = 0, None
    for who in sorted(batches):
        session = roster.session_name(who)
        numbers = ", ".join(label(w["d"]) for w in batches[who])
        text = message(*[[w["line"] for w in batches[who]
                          if w["d"].kind == kind]
                         for kind in ("turn", "notice", "relook")])
        if not send:
            out("WOULD SEND to %s:\n%s" % (session, text.rstrip("\n")))
            continue
        # A relay that didn't answer isn't asked again this run.
        problem = down or post(session, text)
        if problem.startswith(UNREACHABLE) if problem else False:
            down = problem
        if problem:
            failed += 1
            out("NOT SENT to %s: %s; %s stay due" % (session, problem,
                                                      numbers))
        else:
            out("SENT to %s: %s" % (session, numbers))
        for w in batches[who]:
            d = w["d"]
            extra = {"actions": w["actions"]} if w["actions"] else {}
            log.append(journal(d, w["line"], "not sent: " + problem
                               if problem else "sent", session=session,
                               **extra))
            if problem:
                stayed += 1
                held.add(item_key(d))
                continue
            delivered += 1
            entry = dict(key_of(d), woken_at=merger.iso(when))
            count = reminders_sent(w["entry"]) + 1 \
                if w["why"] == "reminder" else 0
            if count:
                entry["reminders"] = count
            record(items, d, entry)
    prune(items, live, only, held)
    out("%s %d open, %d turn(s) to wake%s%s%s%s" % (
        "ROUTED" if send else "DRY-RUN", len(prs) + len(issues),
        sum(len(b) for b in batches.values()),
        ", " + tally if tally else "",
        "; %d wake(s) not sent" % failed if failed else "",
        "; %d withdrawn on recheck" % withdrawn_n if withdrawn_n else "",
        "; %d not rechecked" % unchecked_n if unchecked_n else ""))
    if send:
        os.makedirs(state_dir, exist_ok=True)
        merger.save_json(state_path, state)
        append_records(os.path.join(state_dir, "wakes.jsonl"), log, when)
    else:
        record_dry_run(state_dir, decisions, would, only, when)
    if not stayed:
        return 0
    return 1 if delivered else 2


def append_records(path, records, when):
    if not records:
        return
    with open(path, "a") as handle:
        for record in records:
            record["at"] = merger.iso(when)
            handle.write(json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True) + "\n")


def record_dry_run(state_dir, decisions, would, only, when):
    """Append each turn a dry run would send or withhold to
    `dry-run.jsonl`, once per turn key: `dry-state.json` remembers the
    keys last recorded per item key, in `state.json`'s form, apart from
    the real state, which a dry run never touches."""
    path = os.path.join(state_dir, "dry-state.json")
    seen = merger.load_json(path, {})
    if not isinstance(seen, dict):
        seen = {}
    records = []
    for d, line, outcome in would:
        if find(seen, d) is not None:
            continue
        record(seen, d, key_of(d))
        records.append(journal(d, line, outcome))
    live = {}
    for d in decisions:
        keep = live.setdefault(item_key(d), [])
        if d.kind == "surface" or (d.agent is not None
                                   and d.suppressed is None):
            keep.append(d)
    prune(seen, live, only)
    os.makedirs(state_dir, exist_ok=True)
    merger.save_json(path, seen)
    append_records(os.path.join(state_dir, "dry-run.jsonl"), records, when)


def take_lock(handle, wait_s=LOCK_WAIT_S, sleep=time.sleep,
              clock=time.monotonic):
    """True once `handle` holds an exclusive flock, False after
    `wait_s` seconds of trying."""
    deadline = clock() + wait_s
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            return True
        except OSError:
            if clock() >= deadline:
                return False
            sleep(1)


def parse_only(text):
    try:
        numbers = {int(n) for n in text.split(",") if n.strip()}
    except ValueError:
        numbers = set()
    if not numbers or min(numbers) < 1:
        raise argparse.ArgumentTypeError("--only takes numbers: N[,N]")
    return numbers


def main(argv=None, sh=merger.sh, out=print, post=None, roster=None,
         environ=None, mint=None, directory=None):
    environ = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="forge-router", description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument("--send", action="store_true",
                        help="send the wakes and record them; without it, "
                             "print the decisions and record them in "
                             "dry-run.jsonl")
    parser.add_argument("--only", type=parse_only, metavar="N[,N]",
                        help="route only these issues or pull requests")
    parser.add_argument("--state-dir", default=None,
                        help="where state and records live (default "
                        "~/.local/state/agent-forge/<project>/router)")
    parser.add_argument("--checkout", default=environ.get(
        "FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT"), help="the checkout whose configuration "
        "this reads (default $FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT)")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if not args.checkout:
        out("NO-CONFIG: no --checkout, and FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT is not set")
        return 2
    try:
        project = config.load(os.path.join(
            os.path.expanduser(args.checkout), config.CONFIG_NAME))
    except config.ConfigError as err:
        out("NO-CONFIG: %s" % err)
        return 2
    try:
        configure(project)
    except router.RulesError as err:
        out("BAD-CONFIG: %s" % err)
        return 2
    state_dir = args.state_dir or locks.state_dir(project.name, "router",
                                                  environ)
    try:
        remind_s = int(environ.get("FORGE_ROUTER_REMIND", REMIND_S))
    except ValueError:
        out("BAD-CONFIG: FORGE_ROUTER_REMIND is not a number of seconds")
        return 2
    roster = roster or RULES.Roster(project)
    if post is None and args.send:
        post = make_poster(environ.get("FORGE_ROUTER_RELAY", RELAY),
                           relay_token())
    if directory is None and RULES.wants_directory:
        # A dry run reads it too: reading changes nothing.
        directory = make_directory_reader(
            environ.get("FORGE_ROUTER_RELAY", RELAY), relay_token())
    mint = mint or merger.mint

    def go():
        token = mint(project, ACT_AS)
        if token is None:
            out("NO-TOKEN: could not mint %s's token" % ACT_AS)
            return 2
        try:
            return run(merger.GitHub(token, sh), roster, state_dir,
                       args.send, post, args.only, out, remind_s=remind_s,
                       directory=directory)
        except (RuntimeError, KeyError, TypeError, ValueError) as err:
            out("FAILED: %s" % err)
            return 2

    if not args.send:
        return go()
    os.makedirs(state_dir, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(state_dir, "lock"), "a") as lock:
        if not take_lock(lock):
            out("BUSY: another run held %s for %ds" % (lock.name, LOCK_WAIT_S))
            return 0
        return go()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
